Dataset | ClearMetrics SaaS Financial Analytics

Project Overview

This folder contains the synthetic financial dataset used in the ClearMetrics SaaS Financial Analytics project.

ClearMetrics is a fictional B2B SaaS company offering subscription-based software services to businesses across different industries and geographic regions.

The dataset simulates subscription activity, customer invoicing, and payment transactions to support financial analysis using SQL and Power BI.

Dataset Description

The dataset consists of five CSV files:

customers.csv: Contains customer information, including customer names, industries, and regions.

plans.csv: Contains subscription plan information and monthly pricing.

subscriptions.csv: Contains customer subscriptions and billing cycle details.

invoices.csv: Contains invoice transactions, billing dates, amounts, and statuses.

payments.csv: Contains customer payment transactions and related invoice activity.

Business Context

ClearMetrics operates under a subscription-based business model.

Customers select software subscription plans and are billed according to their subscription arrangements.

The dataset enables analysts to evaluate financial performance, understand customer contributions, and identify patterns in billing and payment activity.

Analytical Applications

The dataset supports several types of analysis:

Monthly invoiced revenue trends

Average invoice values

Customer billing activity

Subscription plan performance

Industry-level financial contributions

Geographic revenue distribution

Customer revenue rankings

Invoice and payment analysis

Data Preparation

The original CSV files were imported into MySQL to create a relational database.

The data was subsequently transformed into a star schema consisting of invoice transactions and supporting dimension tables.

This model was connected to Power BI to support financial reporting and interactive analysis.

Data Disclaimer

This dataset is entirely synthetic.

All customer records, subscription details, invoices, and payment transactions are fictional.

The dataset was created exclusively for educational, analytical, and portfolio demonstration purposes and does not contain actual company financial information.
